PURPOSE OF THIS PROOF OF CONCEPT

This proof of concept documents a defensive approach for detecting and containing automation behavior that resembles command-and-control patterns in Discord environments.

The goal is to demonstrate how server-side monitoring and containment logic can reduce risk when automation is misconfigured or over-privileged.

This PoC focuses on:

* Detection of high-risk behavioral patterns
* Audit-log–based monitoring
* Automated containment strategies
* Least-privilege enforcement
* Safe response design

It does not demonstrate exploitation or destructive activity.



