SUMMARY

This proof of concept demonstrates that command-and-control–like behavior can emerge unintentionally when automation systems combine centralized control with elevated privileges.

By focusing on detection, containment, and architectural safeguards, this work provides a defensive framework to reduce risk and improve resilience in automated systems.

